    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">You are given a list of <var>N</var> integers. For each integer, output its Roman numeral representation, one per line, in the same order as the input. Note: There's a neat trick to this one: Math is welcome.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1</strong>: <var>N</var> (list with number of integers)<br><strong>Next N lines</strong>: one integer per line</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong><var>N</var> lines</strong>, each containing the Roman numeral for the corresponding input value.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; <var>N</var> &le; 20<br>1 &le; value &le; 3999 <br>(standard Roman numeral range, since there's no symbol for 0 or numbers &ge; 4000 without special notation)</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">3\n13\n70\n100</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">XIII\nLXX\nC</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
